SWEET CPUTOP: who eats the CPU (patch 0341, GOAL-LOWCLK lever cpu-witness; R0 log only, reads only, no register access, no hardware write). [obs boot resident-065552-b5] all 5 cores 94-98 % busy while SWEET PROCCPU (0186/0247) knows only backboardd, SpringBoard and Preferences, and its two 'not found' lines are printed once at the first sweetperf tick (1089.069), 32 s before launchd execs either process (exec SpringBoard 1121.394, backboardd 1121.723): the name lookup itself works (bb_pid 301 / sb_pid 303 on 626 later lines), the lines were just early and never followed up. (1) new bsd/dev/sweet_cputop.c: boot-arg sweetcputop=N (period s, 1..60; absent = 1 under sweetperf=1, else off; 0 = off, said): every period one header 'SWEET CPUTOP: t_ms dt_ms procs kthr sum_ms top_ms idle_ms new gone late fail trunc kerr' and at most 8 rows 'SWEET CPUTOP: r R p pid PID ms MS cum_ms CUM name NAME' / 'r R k tid 0xTID ms MS cum_ms CUM cont 0xADDR name NAME' = the processes (proc_iterate + task_info TASK_ABSOLUTETIME_INFO, as 0186/0121) and kernel_task threads (new sweet_cputop_task in osfmk/kern/exception.c: task_lock + thread_info_internal THREAD_BASIC_INFO + thread name + unslid continuation, the walk of 0187) ranked by user+system CPU time used in the period; idle threads never ranked (idle_ms); every drop is counted on the header and named once on a SWEET CPUTOP GAP line (task_info failure, table caps 512 processes / 768 kernel threads, thread walk error); 150000-line cap. (2) kernel threads get names so the rows can be read: sweet_fb_vsync (the vsync timer + panel copy work loop), sweet_usb, sweet_usb_log (the USB log drain), sweet_mali, sweet_touch, sweet_cputop (thread_set_thread_name, osfmk/kern/thread.c). (3) SWEET PROCCPU: backboardd / SpringBoard print a line on every pid change ('not found' when absent, 'pid P (was Q)' when it appears or restarts) instead of one 'not found' at the first tick. Host test tools/test_cputop.py.
